@startuml External-Service State Machine
!define CONDITION [condition]
!define EVENT event
!define RESPONSE / response

title External-Service (React SPA)\nRequest Flow State Machine

[*] --> Idle

state "Idle\n(Home Screen)" as Idle
state "FormReady\n(Order Screen)" as FormReady
state "Submitting\n(loading=true)" as Submitting
state "Success\n(result set)" as Success
state "ClientError\n(form validation)" as ClientError
state "NetworkError\n(catch block)" as NetworkError

Idle --> FormReady : User clicks "Create Order"\n/ navigate('/create-order')

FormReady --> ClientError : User clicks Submit\n[!title || !author || pages<=0 || quantity<=0]\n/ setError("fill all fields...")

FormReady --> Submitting : User clicks Submit\n[all fields valid]\n/ fetch POST to\nhttp://localhost:8080/api/v1/orchestrator/orders\n/ setLoading(true)

Submitting --> Success : HTTP response received\n[res.ok === true && status 200/201]\n/ setResult(data: {orderId, state, createdAt})\n/ reset form state

Submitting --> NetworkError : HTTP response received\n[res.ok === false]\n/ throw Error (caught)\n/ setError(err.message)

Submitting --> NetworkError : fetch() rejects\n[network failure, timeout]\n/ catch(err)\n/ setError(err.message)

Success --> FormReady : Display success message\n/ user sees orderId

ClientError --> FormReady : Display error message\n/ user corrects input

NetworkError --> FormReady : Display error message\n/ user retries

FormReady --> Idle : User navigates home\n/ navigate('/')

note right of Submitting
  Request Body:
  {
    title, author, pages,
    coverType, pageType, quantity
  }

  Code: FunctionMethods.tsx:50-56
end note

note right of Success
  Response:
  {
    orderId: number,
    state: "ORCHESTRATED",
    createdAt: ISO-8601
  }

  Code: FunctionMethods.tsx:59-60
end note

note bottom of NetworkError
  AMBIGUITY: Code throws Error when
  res.ok===false (line 58), so both
  server errors (400/500) and network
  errors end up in same catch block.
  No distinction in current impl.
end note

@enduml
